                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This is an interesting app, but needs a lot more features. First and foremost you need to be able to put a password on a room. I thought this would be an interesting experiment for my students, but they are under 18, and I won't invite them to a completely open room like that just anyone can join. \n\nThe instructor needs to have some controls. Like kicking or muting people if necessary. Also it would be nice if there were some basic avatar controls, even male/female and make choosing colors of clothes to help differentiate. \n\nOculus controls are not good. Hands are rotated strangely, and entering the name doesn't seem to work well. You enter the name, can't click on the save. You can touch the save, but I can't tell if it's actually saved. It just.. closes. If you open it again, there is no name there, so I have no idea if it's really set or not. \n\nMovement is weird. Highlight with A and press B to move after doing so.. never seen those kinds of controls in a game before.\n\nI think this could be a great educational product, but it needs some work. I'll happily revisit my review if they improve it, I'd really like to use this.",
